menu "espOS SignalK"

    config ESPOS_SK_RX_FRAME_MAX
        int "Largest inbound stream frame kept (bytes)"
        default 16384
        range 2048 131072
        help
            Delta messages larger than this are dropped (logged). A
            subscription burst after reconnect (values + meta for many
            paths) can reach several KiB; raise on PSRAM boards that
            subscribe to whole families.

    config ESPOS_SK_NOTIFICATIONS
        bool "Device-health notifications"
        default y
        help
            Let the firmware raise SignalK notifications under
            notifications.espos.<label>.<key> for conditions it can judge
            itself -- memory pressure, a dependency that has gone away --
            via espos_sk_notify().

            Without them such a condition surfaces as a device that has
            quietly stopped working, which looks the same as a hardware
            fault and is the expensive kind of problem to diagnose.

            Turn it off on parts where the RAM matters more: the table is
            allocated on first use, so an unused build already costs
            nothing, but disabling also drops the code and the periodic
            low-memory check.

    config ESPOS_SK_MAX_NOTIFY
        int "Distinct notification keys"
        depends on ESPOS_SK_NOTIFICATIONS
        default 8
        range 1 32
        help
            Slots for remembered notification state, one per key. Allocated
            together on the first notification (~128 bytes each), never
            freed. A firmware's set of conditions is fixed at build time,
            so size this to what it actually raises.

endmenu
